cs': '1736096962000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '437', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4NzU5Mzc2NDY2NzQ5NDgwOTY=', 'text': "I asked ChatGPT to offer a ranking of the best and worst states for teacher qualification. Here's what Chat said: \n\nRankings from Key Sources:\n1. National Council on Teacher Quality (NCTQ)\nNCTQ provides a State Teacher Policy Yearbook that evaluates each state's teacher preparation policies and practices. The rankings from the 2019 Yearbook (which are still relevant today) give a good snapshot of how well-prepared teachers are based on factors like certification requirements, preparation programs, and performance standards.\n\nTop States (Best Prepared Teachers) According to NCTQ:\n\nMassachusetts: Known for rigorous teacher certification requirements, competitive salary, and high standards for teacher preparation.\n\nNew York: Strong teacher preparation programs and a highly competitive certification process.\n\nConnecticut: Well-established teacher preparation programs and strong certification standards.\n\nMinnesota: Rigorous teacher licensing and well-regarded teacher preparation programs.\n\nFlorida: Competitive teacher certification process and an increasing focus on teacher retention.\n\nStates with Strong Preparation, But Room for Improvement:\n\nCalifornia: Although the state has high standards for teacher preparation, the cost of living and salaries often deter potential teachers.\n\nIllinois: Fairly strong teacher preparation programs, but funding and teacher salaries are still issues.\n\nOhio: Improving teacher preparation programs, but there is still a push for more standardized performance metrics for teachers.\n\nVirginia: High-quality programs, but teacher retention is a challenge.\n\nColorado: Generally good preparation but faces challenges related to turnover and funding disparities.\n\nStates with Struggling Teacher Preparation:\n\nLouisiana: While there are improvements, Louisiana’s teacher preparation programs are generally seen as less rigorous, with issues in teacher retention and low salaries.\n\nMississippi: Mississippi faces significant challenges in teacher preparation, including low pay, poor retention, and weaker teacher prep programs.\n\nAlabama: Struggles with low salaries, inadequate teacher prep programs, and high teacher turnover.\n\nSouth Carolina: Struggles with both teacher salaries and the overall quality of teacher preparation programs.\n\nArkansas: Challenges with teacher preparation, certification, and overall teacher quality.\n\n@ChatGPTapp", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '1714438092655149056', 'name': 'ChatGPT', 'screen_name': 'ChatGPTapp', 'indices': [2375, 2386]}]}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Sun Jan 05 16:09:22 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1875914242689290528', 'display_text_range': [14, 284], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 2, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': "@TheChiefNerd I asked ChatGPT to offer a ranking of the best and worst states for teacher qualification. Here's what Chat said: \n\nRankings from Key Sources:\n1. National Council on Teacher Quality (NCTQ)\nNCTQ provides a State Teacher Policy Yearbook that evaluates each state's teacher", 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1875914242689290528', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 0, 'retweet_count'